abindex=3D"-1" data-testid=3D"expandable-text-box">The next wave of AI-enab=
led prop tech in commercial real estate is a tsunami. Those who adopt early=
 will ride it. Those who keep doing the business the old way will get wiped=
 out.
Here=E2=80=99s where I see it hitting first.

We=E2=80=99ve officially entered a new era of technology implementation in =
commercial real estate; and yet, in many ways, we=E2=80=99re still in the v=
ery early innings.

Over the past few years, a lot of new tools have come to market. Some are g=
enuinely helpful. Many are ambitious. A surprising number are trying to be =
all things to all people=E2=80=A6which, in my experience, is rarely where t=
rue breakthroughs actually come from.

The real game-changers are going to be laser-focused, proprietary solutions=
 that solve very specific problems extraordinarily well.

One area I=E2=80=99m particularly excited about is locational intelligence.

For decades, the paradigm was blunt and analog:
You went to the property. You sat and watched people come and go. You talke=
d to store staff. If you were lucky, you got partial sales reports and trie=
d to infer what that meant for performance and risk.

Then came vehicle traffic counts =E2=80=94 a real step forward once departm=
ents of transportation could consistently measure cars.

More recently, we=E2=80=99ve seen the rise of foot-traffic analytics driven=
 by cell-phone pings. That, too, was a leap =E2=80=94 but it=E2=80=99s inhe=
rently limited, and the market is only beginning to fully grapple with thos=
e limitations.

What=E2=80=99s emerging now feels fundamentally different.

We=E2=80=99re starting to see technologies that fuse together massive, hist=
orically siloed data sets native to commercial real estate and apply machin=
e learning, LLMs, and both predictive and generative AI to extract insight =
=E2=80=94 not just observation.

This isn=E2=80=99t about counting bodies.
It=E2=80=99s about understanding behavior, durability, risk, and opportunit=
y at a level that simply wasn=E2=80=99t possible before.

If this trajectory holds =E2=80=94 and I believe it will =E2=80=94 we=E2=80=
=99re on the cusp of something much bigger:
the true democratization of commercial real estate intelligence.

I=E2=80=99ve never been more excited about where this is heading.

